('Why do some experienced consumers prefer lower-testing flower (18-22% THC) over higher-testing flower?', 'They don''t know better', 'Lower-THC flower often has a richer terpene profile, providing a more nuanced and enjoyable experience', 'Lower THC is healthier', 'It''s cheaper', 'B', 'High-THC cultivation sometimes sacrifices terpene complexity. Many connoisseurs find that 18-22% flower with excellent terpenes provides a superior experience to 30%+ flower with a flat profile.', 'cannabis', 'Hard'),
